Employee Attendance and Payroll Processing System
Technical Report: CSENG 407 Final Individual Database Software Project (Project 08)
William V. S. Tubman University, College of Engineering and Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering
Student: Oliver D Toee
Student ID: 35816
Lecturer: Dr. Chris Gilbert
Submission date: 7 December 2026
Database: Supabase PostgreSQL
Repository: https://github.com/diagbadtoee776-debug/employee-attendance-payroll
Abstract
This report describes the design and implementation of an Employee Attendance and Payroll Processing System, built as the final individual project for CSENG 407. The system records and validates daily employee attendance and uses it to calculate simulated payroll for a pay period. The database is a normalized PostgreSQL schema of 14 tables hosted on Supabase. Business rules are enforced inside the database through constraints, exclusion constraints, triggers, an atomic payroll function and Row Level Security, so they hold whichever client connects. A Next.js web application provides login, role-based dashboards and seven modules: employees, attendance, pay setup, payroll runs, payslips, reports and an audit log. The report covers requirements, entity-relationship modelling, functional dependencies and normalization to BCNF, SQL implementation, security with allowed and denied evidence, transactions and concurrency, backup and recovery, object-relational and XML topics, and testing. All data in the project is synthetic.
